---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"Blanc Browser Features — Minimal browsing, built in"}
  description={"Explore the Blanc Island, Glance, built-in blocking, Named Groups, Patron Named Workspaces, Quiet Tabs, local profiles, encrypted sync, and structural security."}
  path="/features"
  page="features"
  current="features"
  ogDescription={"A focused desktop browser with Glance, built-in blocking, Named Groups, Patron Named Workspaces, Quiet Tabs, encrypted sync, and structural security."}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Features", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/features" }
  ]
}
</script>

<main class="feature-page feature-hub-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">features</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--hub" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">the browser, reduced</p>
    <h1 id="features-title">Less browser. More of what you opened it for.</h1>
    <p>Blanc keeps the everyday browser tools close without building a dashboard around them — and ships no AI assistant hovering over any of it. Choose the part of your session you want to make quieter.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-hub-list" aria-label="Blanc browser features">
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="island">
      <p class="feature-number">01</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">the blanc island</p>
        <h2>One small control surface. The whole browser.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Search, tabs, navigation, the current site, and page controls live together, so the page stays in front.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/island" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="island" data-cta-position="feature-hub">Meet the Island <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row feature-hub-row--featured" id="glance">
      <p class="feature-number">02</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">side by side, briefly</p>
        <h2>Open a reference without leaving your place.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Glance opens a temporary page beside the one you are using, then gets out of the way when you are done. It stays local and is never restored or synced.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="ad-blocking">
      <p class="feature-number">03</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">built in</p>
        <h2>Site controls that say what they do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Blanc Blocker stops ads and known trackers at the browser level. Its shield tells you what was blocked here, whether the site uses HTTPS, and lets you turn blocking off for that one site.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/ad-blocking" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="ad-blocking" data-cta-position="feature-hub">See site controls <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="private-tabs">
      <p class="feature-number">04</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">a clean trail</p>
        <h2>Private tabs that stay out of the record.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Private pages do not enter Blanc history, session restore, or reopen-closed. Close the private chip when you are finished.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/private-tabs" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="private-tabs" data-cta-position="feature-hub">Read about private tabs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="commands">
      <p class="feature-number">05</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">keyboard first</p>
        <h2>One shortcut to move through your whole session.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Command or Control L blends open tabs, Favorites, history, and Named Groups. Type / to run browser commands, or reopen a recently closed tab or group without rebuilding your place.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/command-palette" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="command-palette" data-cta-position="feature-hub">Explore commands <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="tab-groups">
      <p class="feature-number">06</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">named groups</p>
        <h2>Name the task. Keep its tabs together.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Named Groups keep related tabs in one cluster. Blanc shows the active group on the Island while the others stay close, folded away from the page.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/tab-groups" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="tab-groups" data-cta-position="feature-hub">Explore Named Groups <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row feature-hub-row--patron" id="workspaces">
      <p class="feature-number">07</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">named workspaces <span class="feature-patron-badge">Patron</span></p>
        <h2>Save a whole window. Return to it by name.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Named Workspaces save a window’s tabs and groups, switch the set in place, and keep it up to date automatically. Active Patrons can create and save them; anything already saved remains available if membership ends.</p>
        <div class="feature-row-actions">
          <a class="feature-patron-cta" data-track="supporter_click" data-feature="named-workspaces" data-cta-position="feature-workspaces" href="https://buy.polar.sh/polar_cl_auwRq39Q2hIVLJwANEqFWgWuZ8DGjdJmEI4mE0JaNDf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">become a Patron</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/about" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="named-workspaces" data-cta-position="feature-hub">what Patron supports <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="vertical-tabs">
      <p class="feature-number">08</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">your preferred view</p>
        <h2>An optional vertical tab rail. The Island stays.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Move tabs to a resizable left rail when a persistent overview helps. Nothing reloads, and the Island remains the only address and command surface.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/vertical-tabs" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="vertical-tabs" data-cta-position="feature-hub">See vertical tabs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="quiet-tabs">
      <p class="feature-number">09</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">memory, on your terms</p>
        <h2>Tabs you are not using give their memory back.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Leave a tab alone and Blanc hands its page back to your computer, then reloads it when you return. You choose the delay; anything half-finished is left awake.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/quiet-tabs" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="quiet-tabs" data-cta-position="feature-hub">How quiet tabs work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="sync">
      <p class="feature-number">10</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">profiles, windows, devices</p>
        <h2>Separate contexts without losing continuity.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Keep browsing identities separate with local profiles and open more than one Blanc window. From Personal, opt-in sync shows what each device has open — end-to-end encrypted, read-only, and never one merged live session.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/sync" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="sync" data-cta-position="feature-hub">How tab sync works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-hub-row" id="security">
      <p class="feature-number">11</p>
      <div>
        <p class="feature-label">private by architecture</p>
        <h2>Security that is structural, not bolted on.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-row-end">
        <p>Sandboxed pages, pinned network-level blocking, signed releases, device-bound Touch ID passkeys, and optional user-invoked 1Password fill on macOS. The quiet parts, documented.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/security" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="security" data-cta-position="feature-hub">Read the security story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-patron" aria-labelledby="feature-patron-title">
    <div class="feature-patron-copy">
      <p class="section-kicker">Patron</p>
      <h2 id="feature-patron-title">Keep the browser free. Get more room to move.</h2>
      <p>Blanc’s core stays free. Patron adds cross-platform Named Workspaces and three macOS Dock colorways while helping fund an independent browser.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-patron-offer">
      <p class="feature-patron-price"><strong>$30</strong><span> / year</span></p>
      <p>or $4 monthly</p>
      <a class="cta" data-track="supporter_click" data-feature="patron" data-cta-position="feature-patron-close" href="https://buy.polar.sh/polar_cl_auwRq39Q2hIVLJwANEqFWgWuZ8DGjdJmEI4mE0JaNDf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">become a Patron</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/about" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="patron" data-cta-position="feature-patron-close">what Patron supports <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="feature-close-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">ready when you are</p>
    <h2 id="feature-close-title">A quieter browser is a small download away.</h2>
    <a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="feature-hub" data-cta-position="feature-hub-close">choose your download</a>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
